<tool id="ampvis2_merge_replicates" name="ampvis2 merge replicates" version="0.1.0+galaxy0" profile="22.09">
  <description>merge replicate samples</description>
  <macros />
  <xrefs>
    <xref type="bio.tools">ampvis2</xref>
  </xrefs>
  <requirements>
    <requirement type="package" version="1.4.0">R</requirement>
    <requirement type="package" version="1.4.0">r-base</requirement>
    <requirement type="package" version="1.4.0">r-ampvis2</requirement>
  </requirements>
  <version_command>Rscript '$__tool_directory__/get_version.R'</version_command>
  <command detect_errors="exit_code">
Rscript '$__tool_directory__/run.R'
--input '$input_rds'
--metadata '$metadata_list'
--output '$output_plot'
--format '$plot_format'
    </command>
  <inputs>
    <param argument="--input" type="data" format="rds" label="Ampvis2 RDS dataset" />
    <param argument="--metadata" type="data" format="tabular" label="Metadata list" />
    <param argument="--format" type="select" label="Plot format">
      <option value="html" selected="true">HTML</option>
      <option value="png">PNG</option>
      <option value="svg">SVG</option>
    </param>
  </inputs>
  <outputs>
    <data name="output_plot" format="html" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Rank abundance plot" />
  </outputs>
  <tests>
    <test>
      <param name="input_rds" ftype="rds" value="subset_sample.rds" />
      <param name="metadata_list" ftype="tabular" value="metadata_subset.csv" />
      <param name="plot_format" value="html" />
      <output name="output_plot" file="rank_abundance_plot.html" compare="sim_size" />
    </test>
  </tests>
  <help>
What it does
============

Aggregates read counts in replicate samples by calculating the mean abundances of OTU's

The Galaxy tool calls the `amp_mergereplicates
&lt;https://kasperskytte.github.io/ampvis2/reference/amp_merge_replicates.html&gt;`_ function
of the ampvis2 package.

Input
=====


        An ampvis2 RDS dataset obtained by the ``ampvis2: load`` tool (or ``ampvis2: mergereplicates`` or one of the
        ``ampvis2: subset ...`` tools).



        The metadata list output of the ``ampvis2: load`` tool (or ``ampvis2: mergereplicates`` or the
        ``ampvis2: subset sample`` tool).  This input is only used for providing
        values to the parameters alowing to select metadata variables or values.


Output
======

An rank abundance plot in the chosen output format.
    </help>
